<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Guided Föhr–Amrum Wadden crossing — Guided Föhr–Amrum full mapped planning course to Norddorf centre [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>Start at Dunsum Deichparkplatz “Zum Wattenläufer” on Föhr for the booked guided crossing toward Amrum’s northern tip. The guide chooses the safe line across sandbanks and tidal channels for that departure. After the crossing, continue along the dune edge to the boardwalk and bicycle parking, take the existing narrow path across the great dune to the open sea, then walk along the beach to Himmelsleiter. Follow the boardwalk across the dunes and continue along Düüwdääl, Lunstruat and Taft to the bus stop in Norddorf village centre. Confirm the separate bus and ferry return arrangements; a bicycle return is an optional transport choice.

A responsible guide and confirmed departure are essential for the tidal crossing. Never attempt it independently or use the historical displayed line for navigation. Channels, water depth, cold water, soft ground, wind, visibility and thunderstorms affect safety; the guide’s current tide, weather and ground assessment governs the route. Departures can change or be cancelled. Recheck arrangements with the operator before travelling.

Follow the operator’s footwear and clothing instructions. The current guide requires suitable neoprene, water, surf or training shoes for the shell-covered final tidal section. Be prepared for prolonged uneven walking and substantial water crossings. Confirm suitability and all equipment with the guide when booking.

Use designated walking paths, dune crossings and boardwalks; do not walk across protected dunes away from the permitted paths. Keep dogs leashed, avoid disturbance during the March–September bird breeding period, and keep at least 200 metres from seals. Obey current signs and manager or guide restrictions. If any required tidal, beach, dune or village-arrival leg is prohibited, closed, unsafe or cancelled, the complete itinerary is unavailable.

The original approximate planning figures are 10 km and 210 minutes with approximate zero ascent and descent. They are variable tide-and-logistics estimates, not the measured length of the displayed full course. The complete mapped walking line, including the beach, dune crossings and Norddorf village arrival, measures about 13.634 km. Actual distance and time depend on the guide’s safe tidal course and conditions. No surveyed elevation profile is supplied.

Historical planning geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright, under the Open Database License 1.0, https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. The tidal alignment was surveyed in 2019 and retained in its 2020 source version; it is not a current field survey or navigation authority. Planning only; GPX navigation and download are disabled.

